          "text": "`max-turns` (default `500`, legacy alias `max-runs`) and `max-ai-credits` (default `1000`) are top-level frontmatter fields supported by all engines. `engine.max-turns` is a deprecated nested alias that still limits Claude iterations when present; `max-continuations` enables Copilot continuation mode. Claude and Codex have native web search support; Codex requires explicit `tools: web-search:` configuration. Copilot and Gemini can use a third-party MCP server for search. Top-level `plugins` is experimental, uses the [Agent Plugins](https://agent-plugins.org) format, and is supported by Copilot, Claude, Codex, and any imported engine definition that declares a `behaviors.plugins` block (such as the shared Cursor and Kiro engines). See [Using Web Search](/gh-aw/reference/web-search/) and [Agent Plugins](/gh-aw/reference/frontmatter/#agent-plugins-plugins)."
